#N canvas 60 60 940 700 12;
#X text 300 20 ligase_primase.pd -- primase = master rhythm clock and ligase~ = the granular voice it triggers. See Plans/web_build.md Arc B (B1/B2). Hand-authored -- primase is an external \, outside the panel_layout.py model. Needs the primase and ligase~ externals on the search path.;
#X obj 40 90 loadbang;
#X msg 560 90 \; pd dsp 1;
#X obj 40 640 ligase~;
#X obj 360 540 noise~;
#X obj 360 250 primase 120;
#X obj 40 130 delay 100;
#X msg 40 160 recinput;
#X obj 40 210 delay 1100;
#X msg 40 240 record 0 \, playhead 1 \, delay_quantize 4 \, delay_quant 1 \, stut_reps 4;
#X obj 220 130 delay 1150;
#X msg 220 160 tempo 120 \, grid 4 \, tap_at 0 \, tap_at 0.25 \, tap_at 0.5 \, tap_at 0.75 \, loop 1;
#X obj 40 300 delay 1250;
#X msg 40 330 play 1;
#X obj 220 210 delay 1350;
#X msg 220 240 play;
#X msg 360 360 stut;
#X msg 500 360 grainstart \$1;
#X msg 640 360 amplitude \$1;
#X obj 360 460 print PRIMASE_EV;
#X obj 40 690 dac~;
#X text 470 250 [primase 120] -- 120 BPM \, 4 beats/cycle => 2000 ms cycle. 4 taps at 0/0.25/0.5/0.75 => a bang every 500 ms.;
#X text 470 460 outlet 0 = bang/event -> stut plus ligase clock bang. outlet 1 = position 0-1 -> grainstart (playhead). outlet 2 = velocity -> amplitude.;
#X text 40 380 One-shot note: primase's bang can drive [play 1( instead of [stut( for rhythmic transport re-triggering (loop 0).;
#X text 40 430 CLOCK-LOCK: each primase bang is also ligase's main-inlet clock bang. With delay_quant on \, stut prints its spacing quantized to the BPM grid ligase derives from primase's 500 ms interval (=> 500.00 ms at 120 BPM).;
#X connect 1 0 6 0;
#X connect 1 0 8 0;
